{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkBpRs4yVHZNBumiKDie35","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu API workout_doc step hr target \"units\" \"%lthr\" start end bpm JSON format\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"HR target workouts broken on Edge 840 firmware ≥30.18 — interpreted as %HRmax instead of bpm\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090\"},{\"title\":\"pkg.go.dev\",\"url\":\"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/tomdiekmann/icu\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Workout builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609\"}]\n\nThe search turned up forum posts and a bug report, but no official schema listing the valid `hr` units, so I couldn't confirm whether `%lthr` is accepted.\n\n- **HR step format:** A bug report includes a working-looking example where an HR step uses a `hr` object with `start`, `end`, and `units: \"bpm\"` inside `workout_doc` ([source](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090)).\n- **Power comparison:** Power steps use a `power` object with `value` and `units` such as `%ftp` ([source](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129)). The HR equivalent appears to follow the same pattern, but that is my inference.\n- **Resolved ranges:** Exported workouts carry a resolved `_power` object with `start` and `end`. The default range is 1.5% for HR, and a `hrRange` query parameter can change it ([source](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20)).\n- **LTHR and max HR:** Developers added `lthr` and `max_hr` fields to the export, so an LTHR-based conversion is possible on the client side ([source](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129)).\n- **Known problem:** A Garmin Edge 840 on firmware 30.18 or later reportedly read bpm HR targets as a percentage of max HR, producing alarms far above the intended range. The same report says public export endpoints drop HR-bpm targets entirely ([source](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090)).\n- **Limited HR support:** A forum reply says HR is not supported as a secondary target alongside power, and only cadence is ([source](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839)).\n\nFor the exact valid `units` values, check the official intervals.icu API docs or test a POST against your own account.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e20a8fa-0f50-4736-b5ef-2d21f37edc90","uuid":"02b3c076-8ce4-426d-86f4-18663b4b9568","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:46:10.183Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu API workout_doc step hr target \"units\" \"%lthr\" start end bpm JSON format","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HTFHC4PwzrAskyj98J2h1c","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-interval