{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRybXSV2aHQC7RKEXVpn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400,"cache_read_input_tokens":28538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":400},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e20a8fa-0f50-4736-b5ef-2d21f37edc90","uuid":"0eb618f6-b6ba-4911-9bae-f78ba19248c6","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:46:20.097Z","request_id":"req_011CgRybXD66mE5fBAa4YXa7","thinking_duration_ms":363,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRybXSV2aHQC7RKEXVpn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JumTcJMpgtjykFqxaAuEfh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-P5COqf/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR targets clamped to watch zones — fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` emitted HR targets as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}` and\nleft the conversion to Intervals.icu at export. The export to Garmin then\nmapped those percentages onto the watch's own zone bands, so every corridor\nshowed up as a zone edge (118–137, 137–151, …) rather than the planned range.\nChanging the watch's LTHR only moved the bands.\n\n## Change (`gen.py`)\n\n- Added `LTHR = 172` (the athlete's LTHR, per README.md) with a comment on why.\n- `hr_target()` now converts each plan percentage to absolute bpm:\n  `start = round(172 * lo / 100)`, `end = round(172 * hi / 100)`, with\n  `\"units\": \"bpm\"`.\n- The `hr` key names changed from `value`/`end` to `start`/`end`, which is the\n  form the Intervals forum shows for bpm HR targets.\n\nGenerated targets for `plans/tempo-run.json`:\n\n| step | planned (% LTHR) | generated (bpm) | matches watch-notes \"expected\" |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 68–75 | 117–129 | yes |\n| Tempo | 88–93 | 151–160 | yes |\n| Float | 75–82 | 129–141 | yes |\n| Cool-down | 65–72 | 112–124 | yes |\n\n## Not verified\n\n- **Not pushed.** I did not POST anything to Intervals. `readback/` still holds\n  the old `%lthr` payload for event 184233.\n- **Not checked on the watch.** I have no device access. The `start`/`end` +\n  `bpm` shape comes from a forum bug report, not the official API schema, so\n  it needs one push to a test event and a look at the Forerunner before\n  trusting it.\n- **Earlier bpm attempt.** The notes say `units: \"bpm\"` with absolute values\n  once showed 214–249 bpm. I don't know which keys or values that attempt used,\n  so I can't rule out the same problem. If the watch shows wrong numbers again,\n  check the exact payload that was sent and whether the Garmin export treats\n  bpm targets as % of max HR (a known problem on some Garmin firmware).\n- **LTHR is hard-coded.** If the athlete's LTHR changes in Intervals, update\n  `LTHR` in `gen.py` too.\n\n## Next step\n\nPush the regenerated event (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json`,\nthen `./push.sh event.json`) to a test athlete or test date, then compare the\nwatch display with the table above.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400,"cache_read_input_tokens":28538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":400},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e20a8fa-0f50-4736-b5ef-2d21f37edc90","uuid":"91ffd20d-7d66-4c46-be91-71c556048c95","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:46:23.843Z","request_id":"req_011CgRybXD66mE5fBAa4YXa7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JumTcJMpgtjykFqxaAuEfh":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-P5COqf/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR targets clamped to watch zones — fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` emitted HR targets as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}` and\nleft the conversion to Intervals.icu at export. The export to Garmin then\nmapped those percentages onto the watch's own zone bands, so every corridor\nshowed up as a zone edge (118–137, 137–151, …) rather than the planned range.\nChanging the watch's LTHR only moved the bands.\n\n## Change (`gen.py`)\n\n- Added `LTHR = 172` (the athlete's LTHR, per README.md) with a comment on why.\n- `hr_target()` now converts each plan percentage to absolute bpm:\n  `start = round(172 * lo / 100)`, `end = round(172 * hi / 100)`, with\n  `\"units\": \"bpm\"`.\n- The `hr` key names changed from `value`/`end` to `start`/`end`, which is the\n  form the Intervals forum shows for bpm HR targets.\n\nGenerated targets for `plans/tempo-run.json`:\n\n| step | planned (% LTHR) | generated (bpm) | matches watch-notes \"expected\" |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 68–75 | 117–129 | yes |\n| Tempo | 88–93 | 151–160 | yes |\n| Float | 75–82 | 129–141 | yes |\n| Cool-down | 65–72 | 112–124 | yes |\n\n## Not verified\n\n- **Not pushed.** I did not POST anything to Intervals. `readback/` still holds\n  the old `%lthr` payload for event 184233.\n- **Not checked on the watch.** I have no device access. The `start`/`end` +\n  `bpm` shape comes from a forum bug report, not the official API schema, so\n  it needs one push to a test event and a look at the Forerunner before\n  trusting it.\n- **Earlier bpm attempt.** The notes say `units: \"bpm\"` with absolute values\n  once showed 214–249 bpm. I don't know which keys or values that attempt used,\n  so I can't rule out the same problem. If the watch shows wrong numbers again,\n  check the exact payload that was sent and whether the Garmin export treats\n  bpm targets as % of max HR (a known problem on some Garmin firmware).\n- **LTHR is hard-coded.** If the athlete's LTHR changes in Intervals, update\n  `LTHR` in `gen.py` too.\n\n## Next step\n\nPush the regenerated event (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json`,\nthen `./push.sh event.json`) to a test athlete or test date, then compare the\nwatch display with the table above.\n"}}}
