k at the Forerunner before\n  trusting it.\n- **Earlier bpm attempt.** The notes say `units: \"bpm\"` with absolute values\n  once showed 214–249 bpm. I don't know which keys or values that attempt used,\n  so I can't rule out the same problem. If the watch shows wrong numbers again,\n  check the exact payload that was sent and whether the Garmin export treats\n  bpm targets as % of max HR (a known problem on some Garmin firmware).\n- **LTHR is hard-coded.** If the athlete's LTHR changes in Intervals, update\n  `LTHR` in `gen.py` too.\n\n## Next step\n\nPush the regenerated event (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json`,\nthen `./push.sh event.json`) to a test athlete or test date, then compare the\nwatch display with the table above.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JumTcJMpgtjykFqxaAuEfh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRybuazjVGqY6gL8vxVN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed the generator so it emits absolute bpm targets instead of `%lthr`, and wrote the details to `ANSWER.md`. I have not confirmed the fix on the watch, and I did not push anything.\n\n**Cause:** `gen.py` sent `%lthr` targets and left the conversion to Intervals' export. The export maps those onto the watch's own zone bands, which is why every corridor showed up as a zone edge.\n\n**Change in `gen.py`:** I added `LTHR = 172` and `hr_target()` now converts each plan percentage to bpm (`round(172 * pct / 100)`), with `\"units\": \"bpm\"` and `start`/`end` keys. The generated values for `plans/tempo-run.json` are:\n\n| step | generated (bpm) |\n|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 117–129 |\n| Tempo | 151–160 |\n| Float | 129–141 |\n| Cool-down | 112–124 |\n\nThese match the \"expected on watch\" column in `readback/watch-notes.md`. The file compiles.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- The `start`/`end` + `bpm` shape comes from a forum bug report, not the official API schema. The forum post is at https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090.\n- The notes say an earlier bpm attempt showed 214–249 bpm. I don't know what that attempt sent, so the same problem could recur. If it does, the Garmin export may be reading bpm as a percentage of max HR.\n- `LTHR` is hard-coded to 172, so it needs updating if the athlete's LTHR changes in Intervals.\n\n**Next step:** push the regenerated event to a test date and compare the watch display with the table in `ANSWER.md`. I left `readback/` unchanged, so it still holds the old payload."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1132,"cache_read_input_tokens":28938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephe